{
  "id": "ss.fx.smear",
  "name": "Smear",
  "description": "The ground a whirled feeler sweeps — Cowboy's turn (ss.char.arin `cast_evo`). Its reach is the drawing's: the lash runs from the body out to the rim, the rim's outer edge sits on `authoredR`, and the sweep fills everything between, because the turn cuts the whole disc and not a ring at its edge. The lead is at 0° and the tail trails back anticlockwise in three held bands, faint to fainter; the engine turns it to wherever the lash is and draws it once, at the radius the turn really has (drawAsset), with `turn` at the turn's progress — a band shows only once the lash has gone all the way past it, and the last fifth lets go in two held steps. Cold and cut-paper: the lines sit on ink, the fill is a tint with none under it, never lit.",
